<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Zboriv</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1649</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmelnytsky-uprising">Khmelnytsky Uprising</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Zboriv was concluded in August 1649 between the Polish king John II Casimir and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">hetman</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a>, after a Polish army had been besieged at Zbarazh and the king's relief force was attacked at Zboriv. It recognised Cossack self-rule in the provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, Bratslav and Chernihiv and raised the Cossack register to 40,000 men. Neither side was satisfied, and war resumed in 1651.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-zboriv.jpg" alt="Treaty of Zboriv" width="320" height="269" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vitaliyf261 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_Zaporizhian_Host.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
